    "changes": [],
    "description": "<p><i>Reference Book: <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Star_Wars_Saga_Edition_Scum_and_Villainy\" title=\"Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy\">Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy</a> </i></p><p><b>Emplacement Points:&nbsp;</b> 2</p><p><b>Size Restriction:&nbsp;</b> Gargantuan or Colossal</p><p>A popular modification for tramp freighters and bounty hunter <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Starfighters\" title=\"Starfighters\">Starfighters</a>, a Cockpit Ejection System allows a ship's cockpit to eject in the event of the ship's destruction, and subsequently act as an <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Escape_Pod\" title=\"Escape Pod\">Escape Pod</a>. When the Starship is destroyed, the <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Pilot_(Vehicle_Combat)\" title=\"Pilot (Vehicle Combat)\">Pilot</a> makes a DC 20 <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Pilot\" title=\"Pilot\">Pilot</a> check. If the check is successful, the cockpit ejects without its inhabitants taking any damage from the destruction of their ship. On a failed check, those within the cockpit take half the damage that exceeds the ship's <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Damage_Threshold\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Damage Threshold\">Damage Threshold</a>, as normal, before the cockpit manages to separate.</p>",
